OBForceField: initialise pointer and logging members, so heap instances are safe

The plugin constructor (MAKE_PLUGIN) initialises no OBForceField data
member, and of the force fields only MMFF94's constructor nulls some.
The registered plugin objects are globals, so zero-initialised; an
instance from MakeNewInstance() is on the heap and starts with garbage
_grad1, _gradientPtr, _velocityPtr, _logos and _loglvl, which the
two-argument Setup(), ConjugateGradientsInitialize() and the destructor
delete[] or log through. Reproduced: a UFF MakeNewInstance() on recycled
heap memory, run with L-BFGS and deleted, dies with
STATUS_HEAP_CORRUPTION; MMFF94 does not. That is the corruption
openbabel_rs saw as "UFF + L-BFGS" and refused the pairing for. Give the
members default initialisers (no layout change).

diff --git a/include/openbabel/forcefield.h b/include/openbabel/forcefield.h
index 5a1939838..fdaac479e 100644
--- a/include/openbabel/forcefield.h
+++ b/include/openbabel/forcefield.h
@@ -524,24 +524,34 @@ const double GAS_CONSTANT = 8.31446261815324e-3 / KCAL_TO_KJ;  //!< kcal mol^-1
     bool IsInSameRing(OBAtom* a, OBAtom* b);
 
     // general variables
+    //
+    // The pointers and the logging state are initialised here, not left to
+    // the constructors: MAKE_PLUGIN's constructor sets none of them and only
+    // MMFF94's sets some. The registered plugin objects are globals, so they
+    // start zeroed anyway; an instance from MakeNewInstance() is on the heap,
+    // and started with a garbage _grad1 / _gradientPtr / _velocityPtr that
+    // Setup(mol, constraints), ConjugateGradientsInitialize() and the
+    // destructor delete[] -- and a garbage _logos / _loglvl to log through.
+    // That corrupted the heap for every force field but MMFF94 (seen as
+    // UFF + L-BFGS).
     OBMol 	_mol; //!< Molecule to be evaluated or minimized
-    bool 	_init; //!< Used to make sure we only parse the parameter file once, when needed
+    bool 	_init = false; //!< Used to make sure we only parse the parameter file once, when needed
     std::string	_parFile; //!< parameter file name
-    bool 	_validSetup; //!< was the last call to Setup successful
-    double	*_gradientPtr; //!< pointer to the gradients (used by AddGradient(), minimization functions, ...)
+    bool 	_validSetup = false; //!< was the last call to Setup successful
+    double	*_gradientPtr = nullptr; //!< pointer to the gradients (used by AddGradient(), minimization functions, ...)
     // logging variables
-    std::ostream* _logos; //!< Output for logfile
+    std::ostream* _logos = nullptr; //!< Output for logfile
     char 	_logbuf[BUFF_SIZE+1]; //!< Temporary buffer for logfile output
-    int 	_loglvl; //!< Log level for output
-    int 	_origLogLevel;
+    int 	_loglvl = OBFF_LOGLVL_NONE; //!< Log level for output
+    int 	_origLogLevel = OBFF_LOGLVL_NONE;
     // conformer genereation (rotor search) variables
     int 	_current_conformer; //!< used to hold i for current conformer (needed by UpdateConformers)
     std::vector<double> _energies; //!< used to hold the energies for all conformers
     // minimization variables
     double 	_econv, _gconv, _e_n1; //!< Used for conjugate gradients and steepest descent(Initialize and TakeNSteps)
     int 	_cstep, _nsteps; //!< Used for conjugate gradients and steepest descent(Initialize and TakeNSteps)
-    double 	*_grad1; //!< Used for conjugate gradients and steepest descent(Initialize and TakeNSteps)
-    unsigned int _ncoords; //!< Number of coordinates for conjugate gradients
+    double 	*_grad1 = nullptr; //!< Used for conjugate gradients and steepest descent(Initialize and TakeNSteps)
+    unsigned int _ncoords = 0; //!< Number of coordinates for conjugate gradients
     int         _linesearch; //!< LineSearch type
     //! Hidden L-BFGS history. Forward-declared here (full definition lives
     //! in forcefield.cpp behind HAVE_EIGEN3) to keep Eigen out of this header
@@ -559,7 +569,7 @@ const double GAS_CONSTANT = 8.31446261815324e-3 / KCAL_TO_KJ;  //!< kcal mol^-1
     // molecular dynamics variables
     double 	_timestep; //!< Molecular dynamics time step in picoseconds
     double 	_temp; //!< Molecular dynamics temperature in Kelvin
-    double 	*_velocityPtr; //!< pointer to the velocities
+    double 	*_velocityPtr = nullptr; //!< pointer to the velocities
     // contraint varibles
     static OBFFConstraints _constraints; //!< Constraints
     static unsigned int _fixAtom; //!< SetFixAtom()/UnsetFixAtom()
